> Note that temporarily enabling debug on a live endpoint isn't a big issue=
,=0A=
> everything will continue to operate as before except for the one client t=
hat=0A=
> requests debug-level alerts, and that knows what it's up for because it=
=0A=
> explicitly asked for it.=0A=
=0A=
And for the malicious user that, knowing the server is currently in debug m=
ode and returning extended errors, can more easily perform attacks on it...=
=0A=
